  ('bed280c4-debb-5c43-8213-aa84b4dd0bfe', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants to replace sentence 7 with dialogue that moves the story forward. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"This box is made of metal,\" Principal Nakamura said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-old-detail"},{"text":"Principal Nakamura unfolded a yellowed page. \"Listen to this,\" the principal said, and began to read.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Please go back to your classrooms now,\" Principal Nakamura said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-events"},{"text":"\"Good morning, students,\" Principal Nakamura said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-no-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Principal Nakamura unfolded a yellowed page. "Listen to this," the principal said, and began to read.$q$, $q$This choice shows the principal starting to read, which leads straight into Ruthie's letter in sentences 8 and 9. Sending the students back to class would not fit, because they stay to hear the letter and laugh.$q$, 'draft', '7daaee56-74b9-5cdd-af42-a6b11d4ff7d9')
